# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING IN THIS REPO AUTO-LOADS .env. There is no dotenv; the dependency list
# is empty on purpose. Copying this file to .env is NOT enough on its own.
#
# Either pass Node's built-in flag on every launch (Node 22+):
#     node --env-file=.env spire-demo/server.mjs
#
# ...or skip .env entirely and write the key to .private/typesafe.cfg, which
# every entrypoint reads automatically with no flag:
#     api_key = "sk-or-v1-..."
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Jev is reached through OpenRouter's decisions endpoint:
#   POST https://openrouter.ai/api/alpha/decisions   model: typesafe/jev-1.13
# It is NOT a chat-completions model and will not work through a chat client.
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys — it starts with "sk-or-v1-".
#
# Both variables below take the SAME OpenRouter key. They are not
# interchangeable, because different entrypoints read different names:
#
#   TYPESAFE_API_KEY    server.mjs (the app you run), benchmark/run.mjs,
#                       benchmark/run-sequences.mjs, evaluate-plans.mjs
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY  benchmark/sweep.mjs, benchmark/vs-llm.mjs
#
# Everything except vs-llm.mjs falls back to .private/typesafe.cfg, so
# vs-llm.mjs is the only script that truly requires an environment variable.
# Setting both to the same key is the simplest thing that works.

TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional runtime flags (defaults shown)
# SPIRE_SINGLE_CALL=1    # single-call factored decisions. Unset = upstream multi-call policy
# SPIRE_HEDGE=1          # set to 0 to disable request hedging
# SPIRE_PLAN_BENEFIT=1   # enable the plan-benefit scoring path
# PORT=4317              # dashboard port
# MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=      # stop threshold for a run
# MAX_DECISIONS=         # stop after N decisions
